A||N||27||AusFiero||Surgery date is set - I am home on day leave||||1||
Z||000000||AusFiero||07-11-2001||10:42 AM||||Well I have finally found out more about my tumour. Not malignent as far as they can tell anyway. But very very very slim chance of that. Also my surgeon informed me he has a success rate of 95% of people coming out of it with no major disability with his 10 years of doing these ops. At worse I am probably not going to be able to feel the side of my face on the left side and may have some difficulty swallowing or may have some wierd feelings in my left side for life. But hey...life is the operative word and much better than other options  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I was allowed to come home tonight so I can spend a day with my kids tomorrow and then I go back into hospital tomorrow arvo. Surgery is Friday and will take about 5 hours.<P>After that I am looking at 2 days in intensive care then another week in hospital. When I come home I have to then rest for 6 weeks. <P>I will have a golf ball size hole in the lower left of my skull but they said they will not put a plate as it is covered by muscles and won't need it. He has done the same op to a pro footballer who still plays to this day with the same hole. <P>So my spirits are up big time now and I am very happy even with impending extended recovery time. <P>Thanks for the flood of email well wishes, they really do mean a lot to me. Monkeyman will be keeping in contact with my wife and will be able to give updates on my progress.<P>Cheers all and keep on Fieroing.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
